# Sanctioned standard-library files that may call errors.New(...) despite the
# stdlib-error-rooting rule (see stdlib-error-rooting.sh).  One
# <repo-relative-file> per line; comments start with #.
#
# Use this ONLY for a genuine, reviewed exception.  A stdlib error normally must
# root in a base — errors.Rooted(base, msg), errors.Wrap(cause, msg), or return a
# base directly — so a new errors.New(...) in the stdlib almost always means the
# error should instead be rooted in one of the errors.bni bases.
#
# No exceptions today: the errors package itself (which defines the base
# singletons via New) is exempted structurally by the check, not listed here.
